<h1>Manufacturing</h1>
<p class="story-lead">Maintenance at the plant was split between the floor and the office. The people beside the line could not see the status the planner had already updated.</p>
<p>An audit, an AMC visit, and a breakdown on the same asset were three separate lists. The office closed a job that the floor still had open.</p>
<p>They tied maintenance, audits, and vendor visits to the asset. The floor and the office now read one status, and the next AMC visit starts from the last one instead of a fresh sheet.</p>
